values ('ap_physics_1', 2, '2.2', array['2.2']::text[], 'diagram', 'Free-body diagram (FBD)', 'A single-object or single-system diagram that shows every force the environment exerts on it, drawn as separate straight arrows starting on the center-of-mass dot.', '[{"label": "Dot", "meaning": "Represents the object or system''s center of mass; all force arrows originate here."}, {"label": "Force arrows", "meaning": "Each force exerted on the object by the environment is its own straight arrow starting on the dot and pointing in the direction of the force."}, {"label": "Same-direction forces", "meaning": "Forces pointing the same way are drawn side by side, not overlapping."}, {"label": "Whole forces only", "meaning": "Depict the forces themselves, not force components."}, {"label": "Coordinate axis", "meaning": "Choose one axis parallel to the direction of acceleration (e.g., parallel to an incline) to simplify translating the diagram to algebra."}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'Draw each force as its own straight arrow originating on the dot and pointing in the direction of the force, and draw forces in the same direction side by side rather than overlapping (Topic 2.2 boundary statement). Depict the forces exerted on the object, not their components.', 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=ap-physics-1-reference-u1-u3-2026-10-10; candidate=ap_physics_1-u2-r3-002; ced=2.2.B.2-2.2.B.4 and boundary statement: ''individual forces represented on a free-body diagram must be drawn as individual straight arrows, originating on the dot''; product-owner-directed correction by the Claude session (David, 2026-10-10): the escalated row was corrected against its own CED evidence and re-checked by both independent checkers and the own-family veto')
