values ('ap_physics_1', 2, '2.6', array['2.6']::text[], 'vocabulary', 'Apparent weight', 'The magnitude of a system''s apparent weight is the magnitude of the normal force exerted on it, which differs from the gravitational force when the system is accelerating.', '[]'::jsonb, NULL, 'A system appears weightless when no forces act on it or when gravity is the only force on it, not because gravity is absent.', 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=ap-physics-1-reference-u1-u3-2026-10-10; candidate=ap_physics_1-u2-r2-009; ced=2.6.C.1 ''The magnitude of the apparent weight of a system is the magnitude of the normal force exerted on the system.''')
